  The reel_script states the victims were 'யோகானந்தம், தீபா மற்றும் மற்றொரு குழந்தை' without identifying the child, and the reel_script says the four people included 'ஒரு குழந்தை' (one child) when the article names two children (Paranikumar, 9, and Durga, 6).
  The reel_script omits the victims' professions (private school teacher and government school teacher), which are facts from the article but are not strictly required; however the reel_script's description of Yoganandam and Deepa lacks ages in the article's context is accurate, so this is minor.
  The draft's slides_spec and caption state the injured child is 'சிறுவன்' (boy) and the dead child is unspecified or 'சிறுமி' (girl); the article identifies Durga (dead) as a girl only by name, so calling her 'சிறுமி' is an inference not stated in the article.
  The caption says 'நான்கு பேருடன்' (with four people) and the reel_script says 'நான்கு பேர்' as the total, which the article supports, but the caption also says 'நேற்று (நவ. 24)' correctly; no date error found there.
